      "verified": false,
      "notes": "Sensor is an OmniVision part, not Sony (Mike, 2026-09-15; specs are public via C-Star and reviews). spcc_sensor stays null on purpose: Siril's SPCC database carries no OmniVision entries at all (Sony, Canon, Nikon, Onsemi, Samsung, Fujifilm only), so there is nothing to name and the colour stage falls through to plain pcc. That fallback is what inverts the Ha/OIII ratio on nebula-filled fields - see the M8 measurement in CLAUDE.md - so the fix for this scope is the fallback, not a sensor string. Native frame and pixel size still unknown; match patterns are guesses."
